<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75384" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρτῠγία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
			ʽὄρτυξ̓</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Quail-island,</i> the ancient
			name of Delos or Rhenaea, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				10.5.5
			</span></i> ; also of other places in Greece ; in one of these Artemis
			killed <i><span class="en">
				Orion
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.123
			</span></i>: hence she is called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρτυγία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				213
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> part
			of the city of Syracuse, otherwise called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νᾶσος,</span> the Island, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				6.2.4
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>